(# Rounded Horner evaluation with a forward-error bound) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Use the supplied abstract relative-error rounding model. Coefficients form) Tj T*
(a finite list of real numbers in increasing degree order. For every such) Tj T*
(list and every real x, construct exact and rounded Horner evaluation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The exact evaluator P returns 0 on the empty list and satisfies) Tj T*
(P\(a :: tail, x\) = a + x * P\(tail, x\).) Tj T*
(The rounded evaluator Q returns 0 on the empty list and satisfies) Tj T*
(Q\(a :: tail, x\) = round\(a + round\(x * Q\(tail, x\)\)\).) Tj T*
(Use one rounded multiplication and one rounded addition per list step.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Construct an error envelope E using only the exact evaluator, x, the) Tj T*
(coefficients, and the model parameter u. The empty-list envelope is 0.) Tj T*
(At a cons step, put v = P\(tail, x\) and e = E\(tail, x, u\). The envelope is) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(u * |a + x*v| + \(1+u\) * \(u * |x*v| + \(1+u\) * |x| * e\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prove |Q\(coefficients, x\) - P\(coefficients, x\)| <= E\(coefficients, x, u\)) Tj T*
(for every supplied model, coefficient list, and x. The model already gives) Tj T*
(u >= 0 and the relative rounding law. The result needs no smallness,) Tj T*
(sign, nonzero-input, or exact-arithmetic hypothesis.) Tj T*
ET
